Audley Street

This is a pleasant street that winds through Mayfair, a fashionable district which takes its name from an ancient fair held there in May of each year.

To the south is Hyde Park Corner, and to the north is Orchard Street.

You can barely see through the thick fog.

The detective trails along after you.

>s
Hyde Park Corner

Hyde Park Corner is dominated by the Wellington Arch, a soaring monument to the "Iron Duke," who defeated Napoleon at the Battle of Waterloo.

The arch is enshrouded in fog.

Roads lead off in many directions.

Your companion follows you and begins pacing back and forth nervously.

