Broad Sanctuary

You are standing in front of the west door of Westminster Abbey. The towers of the Abbey loom in the fog above you, and you marvel at this perfect example of Gothic architecture, as generations have done before you.

The Abbey door is closed.

On the wall next to the door is a small, discreet sign.

Your companion walks alongside you.

>wait until 7:00
Time passes...

Visibility increases in the gathering light of the new day. Tourists are beginning to crowd into the streets.

Do you want to continue waiting?
Please press Y or N > y

While you were waiting, the sun rose... as much as it ever does here.

A verger appears, unlocks the huge door, and pushes it open.

The sun comes up, as much as it ever comes up in England.

In the distance, you hear Big Ben strike the hour.

>turn off lamp
You turn down the wick. The lamp goes dark.

>in
Nave

You enter the Abbey and pause in the Nave, struck by the sheer magnificence of the building. Massive Purbeck columns march the length of the Nave, and they rise in perfect proportion to meet each other in a series of pointed arches that are the hallmark of the Gothic style.

The interior of the Abbey is dark, cold, and gloomy - but after a few moments your eyes adjust and you can make out a tomb at the far end of the room.

Holmes trails along after you.

>s
South Aisle

You enter the South Aisle of the Nave. In the gloom, you bump into one of the tombs. There is an exit to the southeast and a door set into the south wall.

Your friend walks into the room alongside you.

