Holmes leans forward with an excited expression upon his hawk-like features and says, "There is only one man in all London clever enough to plan this, Watson - Professor Moriarty. See how boldly he hides clues in public places, knowing all the while that they will remain hidden from the casual eye. Onward, Doctor. Let us solve these riddles and see what the good Professor has in mind for us."

