Holmes says, "It's obviously not one of the Crown Jewels, Watson. In fact, this gem belongs to the Agra treasure, which was stolen in India many years ago and has never been recovered."

"The case grows more complex, Watson. We are in more danger than I had at first suspected." He removes a ring from one of his long, slender fingers and hands it to you. "Here, Watson. Take this signet ring of mine. If anything should happen to me, take it to my brother Mycroft at the Diogenes Club. He'll tell you what to do."

